From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 08:42:53 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: add the GRX500 watchdog node

SoC-scope node for the new intel_grx500_wdt driver: the GIC local
watchdog interrupt, the CPU clock the countdown runs at, and a phandle to
the RCU syscon, which holds both the register that lets an expiry reach
the chip reset and the bit that says the last reset came from one.

No reg property. The timer's registers are the GIC's VP-local window,
which the driver reaches through the CPS accessors; the vendor node's
reg = <0 0> exists only because its driver called platform_get_resource()
and threw the answer away.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
index 925890e8ee1e..df2d085f7358 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
@@ -108,6 +108,22 @@ reboot {
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * There is no watchdog block on this SoC — the timer is the GIC's
+	 * per-VP watchdog — so this node carries no reg and no unit address.
+	 * The RCU phandle supplies the reset-enable bit and the reset-cause
+	 * word. The interrupt is per-VP and optional.
+	 */
+	watchdog {
+		compatible = "intel,grx500-wdt";
+
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_LOCAL 0 IRQ_TYPE_NONE>;
+		clocks = <&cgu CLK_CPU>;
+		intel,rcu-syscon = <&rcu>;
+		timeout-sec = <30>;
+	};
+
 	asc0: serial@16600000 {
 		compatible = "lantiq,asc";
 		reg = <0x16600000 0x100000>;
